---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { REPO_URL } from '../../lib/constants';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="BluePainter MCP Server"
  description="Install the BluePainter MCP server so AI assistants can analyze TSX ids, evaluate Designer's Receipts and look up product facts."
>
  <section class="section prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">MCP</p>
    <h1>MCP server</h1>
    <p>
      BluePainter ships an MCP server so Claude, Cursor and other assistants can grade a component against
      policy, check which JSX the canvas can map, and look up product facts. Read tools need no credentials;
      tools that call other services need a token where noted.
    </p>
    <h2>Install</h2>
    <p>From a clone of the <a href={REPO_URL}>repository</a>:</p>
    <pre class="code-block"><code>cd mcp && npm install
npx @modelcontextprotocol/inspector node src/index.js</code></pre>
    <h2>Tools</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><code>bluepainter_open_demo</code> — demo deep links</li>
      <li><code>bluepainter_analyze_tsx</code> — count syncable JSX ids</li>
      <li><code>bluepainter_receipts_evaluate</code> — run receipt policy on a node map</li>
      <li><code>bluepainter_get_knowledge</code> — knowledge catalog / FAQ snippets</li>
      <li><code>bluepainter_request_pilot</code> — submit pilot waitlist entry</li>
      <li><code>bluepainter_figma_import</code> — Figma fetch (requires FIGMA_TOKEN)</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Use it from your assistant</h2>
    <p>
      Point your MCP client's server command at <code>node mcp/src/index.js</code> from the repo root. Setup notes
      for each client are in <code>mcp/README.md</code>.
    </p>
    <p class="stack-lg"><a href="/knowledge">← Knowledge catalog</a></p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
